<!DOCTYPE html>
{# ⚠️ S134c: this said `lang="fr"` unconditionally, on every admin page, whatever
   the operator's language. `base_public` has read the locale since it was written;
   this shell never did. It is not cosmetic — `lang` is what a screen reader picks a
   voice from and what a browser offers to translate, so an English admin was being
   read aloud in French. #}
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{% block title %}FabOS{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/style.css') ~ '?v=20260805-s84-surfaces' }}">
    {# Shared member/admin components. Rights state and summaries must render
       identically wherever an operator previews what a member sees. #}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/components.css') ~ '?v=20260809-s98-usage-rights' }}">
    {% block stylesheets %}{% endblock %}
    {# ⚠️ The favicon was in the shell's 46 standalone siblings and NOT here, so
       the 23 pages already extending this file had no icon at all — and a page
       converted to the shell would have lost one. `base_public.html.twig` has
       carried it all along; this is the same line. #}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ asset('images/favicon.png') }}">
    {# AssetMapper — Stimulus seul, Turbo délibérément désactivé (assets/controllers.json).

       ⚠️ Ceci ne remplace PAS les <script src="{{ asset('js/...') }}"> existants et ne
       change RIEN à la navigation : sans Turbo, `importmap()` n'ajoute qu'un module
       différé qui câble les `data-controller`. Le CSS reste dans public/css/ avec son
       cache-buster `?v=` ; ne faites pas passer une feuille de style par AssetMapper,
       elle échapperait au buster.

       ⚠️ Le déploiement a deux étapes de plus à cause de cette ligne :
       `importmap:install` puis `asset-map:compile` (assets/vendor/ et public/assets/
       sont gitignorés, donc le tar ne les transporte pas). #}
    {{ importmap('app') }}
</head>
<body>
{% block body %}{% endblock %}
{% block javascripts %}<script src="{{ asset('js/main.js') ~ '?v=20260811-s134c-i18n' }}"></script>{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
